// caption-video is the FALLBACK. The API's captions endpoint is the default path
// and it belongs to novoads-api, so every positive here carries the reason the API
// path was ruled out: the style, the wording, or a source with no audio track.
{"intent":"burn karaoke style captions in our own brand font, the presets don't have it","expected_skill":"caption-video"}
{"intent":"the transcript is wrong in three places, fix the words first and then burn them in","expected_skill":"caption-video"}
{"intent":"the api refused this file because it was rendered without audio, caption it locally","expected_skill":"caption-video"}
{"intent":"word by word captions in the exact colours from our brand kit","expected_skill":"caption-video"}
{"intent":"caption this without spending anything, the file is already on my machine","expected_skill":"caption-video"}
// Indirect: the constraint is the budget, and free is what makes the local path
// the answer instead of the one-call endpoint.
{"intent":"we're out of credits until Monday but this clip still needs text on it","expected_skill":"caption-video"}
// The bare ask is the API's, offered as two paths. A style the presets cannot
// express is what moves it here.
{"intent":"captions on this, but none of the preset styles are right","expected_skill":"caption-video","ambiguous_with":["novoads-api"]}
// Same file, same operation, different reason: the words have to be read and
// corrected before they are burned into pixels, which the endpoint cannot do.
{"intent":"subtitle this clip, and let me read the text before it goes on","expected_skill":"caption-video","ambiguous_with":["novoads-api"]}
